# ChartQuest — security headers for CLOUDFLARE PAGES  (the file that is ACTUALLY SERVED)
# =============================================================================================
# WHY THIS FILE IS HERE AND NOT AT THE REPO ROOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Pages reads `_headers` from its BUILD OUTPUT DIRECTORY. For playchartquest.com that
# directory is `website/` — NOT the repo root. The root `_headers` has therefore never been read
# by Cloudflare, and from the start of the closed beta until 2026-08-05 the live site sent NO
# Content-Security-Policy, NO HSTS and NO X-Frame-Options at all. Verified with:
#
#     curl -sI https://playchartquest.com/game      → only `x-content-type-options: nosniff`
#
# Proof that production serves website/ (docs/operations/CloudflareDeployment.md §2 says "/ (repo
# root)" and is WRONG):
#   • https://playchartquest.com/sw.js returns `chartquest-site-v12`, i.e. website/sw.js. The ROOT
#     sw.js says 'chart-quest-v325' and is never served — despite its "bump per release" comment.
#   • https://playchartquest.com/ is the marketing landing page (website/index.html), not the game.
#   • The game is https://playchartquest.com/game = website/game.html.
#   • verify.js gate #17 already encodes "production serves website/".
#
# This is the THIRD time one bug class has bitten this project: a correct file that never reaches
# production because of WHERE IT SITS relative to what is actually served. The other two were the
# untracked website/ assets and the boss cinematics that 404'd for ~20 builds. Every local gate was
# green each time. A local check CANNOT see this class — the dev server sends no CSP at all.
# Always verify with `curl -sI` against the live URL.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWO BUGS IN THE ROOT `_headers` THAT ARE DELIBERATELY *NOT* COPIED HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The root policy was never applied, so it was never falsified. Applying it verbatim would have
# broken the site in two ways:
#
#   1. `X-Frame-Options: DENY` + `frame-ancestors 'none'`
#      play.html embeds the game in a SAME-ORIGIN iframe (`#cqGame`, src = 'game.html'). DENY
#      blocks framing even from the same origin, so the Play button would have rendered a blank
#      frame for every player. → SAMEORIGIN / frame-ancestors 'self'.
#
#   2. `style-src 'self'` + `font-src 'self'`
#      game.html loads https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter…, and THAT stylesheet fetches
#      the actual font files from https://fonts.gstatic.com — a host that appears nowhere in the
#      HTML, so it cannot be found by grepping the source. Both origins are required or every
#      glyph falls back.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THE CSP SHIPS AS REPORT-ONLY FIRST
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A wrong CSP breaks the game silently and in production only. The root file's own comments record
# the precedent: omit api.coinbase.com from connect-src and every market falls back to its
# build-time anchor WHILE THE HUD STILL SAYS "live".
#
# So this follows the same observe-then-enforce discipline CQBEAT used: `Content-Security-Policy-
# Report-Only` reports violations to the browser console WITHOUT blocking anything, the live site
# is then walked (landing → play → game → survey) with the console open, and only once that is
# clean does the header get renamed to `Content-Security-Policy`.
# The other five headers below are enforcing immediately — none of them can break this site.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORIGIN ALLOWLIST — every external host the SERVED pages actually load
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   cdn.jsdelivr.net        the Supabase JS SDK (script)
#   *.supabase.co           auth, the beta-ingest edge function, realtime (https + wss)
#   api.coinbase.com        live market prices (Market Identity System)
#   api.binance.com         live market prices (fallback source)
#   fonts.googleapis.com    the webfont STYLESHEET
#   fonts.gstatic.com       the webfont FILES the stylesheet then requests
#   static.cloudflareinsights.com  +  cloudflareinsights.com
#                           Cloudflare Web Analytics. INJECTED BY CLOUDFLARE AT THE EDGE, so it
#                           appears in NO source file — grepping the repo can never find it. Found
#                           only because the Report-Only round reported it from the live site.
#
# 'unsafe-eval' is required, and that is not decoration either. The CQBEAT block (event spacing)
# makes 10 `(0, eval)('market._boxMade = …')` calls to reach the spawners' internal counters — its
# documented runtime-patching design. Enforcing without 'unsafe-eval' would have silently disabled
# CQBEAT's spawn enforcement in production while every local gate stayed green. Drop this directive
# only if those eval calls are ever replaced with direct references.
#
# NOT allowlisted, deliberately — these are referenced but never loaded:
#   www.tradingview.com     an attribution <a href> in index.html. A link is not a fetch.
#   www.apache.org          a licence URL inside a comment in assets/lightweight-charts…js
#   lightweight-charts is bundled LOCALLY under assets/, so it needs no external origin.
#
# 'unsafe-inline' is unavoidable: game.html is one self-contained document with 18 inline <script>
# and 3 inline <style> blocks, and Cloudflare Pages cannot inject a per-response nonce into a
# static file. Removing it would mean un-inlining the game, which is a much larger change.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HSTS: `includeSubDomains` is deliberately OMITTED on this first application
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The root file declares `max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains`. The max-age is kept; the
# includeSubDomains is not, because this is the FIRST time HSTS has ever actually been sent, and
# that directive is a one-way door: browsers cache it for a year and it forces HTTPS on EVERY
# subdomain of playchartquest.com, including any that does not exist yet. The apex — which serves
# the game — is fully protected either way.
# To add it once every subdomain is confirmed HTTPS-only, it is a one-line change here:
#     Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
#
# RULE: any new outbound host must be added HERE first — this is the policy that ships. Keep the
# repo-root `_headers` and netlify.toml in step in the same commit so a future output-directory
# change cannot silently regress the policy.
# =============================================================================================
/*
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.supabase.co wss://*.supabase.co https://api.coinbase.com https://api.binance.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://*.cloudflareinsights.com; img-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; frame-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; object-src 'none'
